[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2521116631","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99975#issuecomment-2521116631","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99975","id":2521116631,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WRS_X","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-05T18:24:38Z","updated_at":"2024-12-05T18:25:35Z","body":"It is indeed strange that PhysicalBone3D can_sleep is true but there is no sleeping property. However, I am not sure if we should add a sleeping property for each classes without extending.\r\n\r\nIs there a reason not to add a sleeping property to PhysicsBody3D? Or maybe we should add an intermediate class like RigidableBody3D between RigidBody3D and PhysicsBody3D and add the sleeping property there.\r\n\r\nSo the decision requires the opinion of the physics team. cc @rburing","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2521116631/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2522645070","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99975#issuecomment-2522645070","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99975","id":2522645070,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WXIJO","user":{"login":"paul-marechal","id":14182238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTgyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14182238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal","html_url":"https://github.com/paul-marechal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T09:33:33Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T09:34:20Z","body":"@TokageItLab I hear you as I also wondered if a refactoring was due.\r\n\r\nBut here's why I think this PR is fine as is:\r\n\r\n- This is my very first contribution to Godot's code base, but also my first contribution to a C++ project at all\r\n- I am not confident enough to carry on a refactor of Node classes\r\n- I submitted this contribution as it is something I need for my own projects\r\n- The refactoring can be deferred for when someone with more experience wants to tackle it\r\n\r\nThis change doesn't add much more debt for when the refactoring will happen: currently is just means there's a little code duplication, and it may actually help direct the effort when refactoring by showing where things need to be shared.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2522645070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2522720488","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99975#issuecomment-2522720488","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99975","id":2522720488,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WXajo","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T10:05:11Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T10:05:11Z","body":"Yes, refactoring can be done later. However, I cannot judge the reasonableness of can_sleep being true and the safety of implementing sleeping, so the decision must be made by the physics team.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2522720488/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2522770592","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99975#issuecomment-2522770592","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99975","id":2522770592,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WXmyg","user":{"login":"paul-marechal","id":14182238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTgyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14182238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal","html_url":"https://github.com/paul-marechal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T10:30:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T15:40:49Z","body":"I'd be happy to hear from the physics team to see if my understanding is correct:\r\n\r\nPhysicalBone3D nodes are regular PhysicsBody3D that are either static or kinematic while following animations, and become rigid when simulating. Something I haven't considered is what happens to the sleeping state when in either static or kinematic mode? I can look into this.\r\n\r\nHowever, when in rigid mode there's most definitely value in having access to the sleeping state: the simulation will eventually settle and we don't want to waste physics resources on non-moving bodies (the physical bones). Once the bones are sleeping I can stop doing whatever processing I was doing on them and only resume when woken up.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2522770592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2799209324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99975#issuecomment-2799209324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99975","id":2799209324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6m2Its","user":{"login":"paul-marechal","id":14182238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTgyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14182238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal","html_url":"https://github.com/paul-marechal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/paul-marechal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2